% The width witness (M1-T30, shape recorded in D-0028).
%
% Until this model existed the widest declared domain in the whole suite was
% `var 0..9`, so the width-proportional cost D-0028 measures was invisible to every
% test: at w = 9 a weakening chain is nine literals and looks like nothing.
%
% Two variables at 0..999 and one row that is infeasible on the DECLARED bounds --
% a + b can reach 1998 and the row demands 2500 -- so the solver refutes it at the
% root having pruned NOTHING and branched NOWHERE. The proof is six lines. One of
% them is 23.8 kB: `Order_reason.weaken_declared` spans each variable's whole
% declared width, and the row it cancels against is the order encoding's own
% expansion, which is Theta(w) literals per variable (D-0028, "the width is inherited
% from the encoding").
%
% Measured here, with veripb 3.0.2, against the same shape at other widths:
%
%   w        .opb      .pbp    longest line   solve   verify
%   9        982 B     303 B      195 B         5 ms    10 ms   <- width_narrow_unsat
%   999      126 kB   23.9 kB    23.8 kB       50 ms    18 ms   <- this model
%   4999     670 kB    128 kB     128 kB      231 ms    59 ms
%   999999   156 MB   29.8 MB    29.8 MB       72 s     12 s    (D-0028, not a test)
%
% w = 999 is the smallest width that makes the effect unmistakable rather than
% merely present: the single `pol` line is 99.5% of the proof and is two orders of
% magnitude larger than any line the rest of the suite emits, while the model still
% costs under a tenth of a second end to end. w = 99 is only a 2.2 kB line, which is
% the same order as an ordinary proof here and would not stand out; w = 4999 costs
% four times as much for a fact already established.
%
% This model is NOT a regression test for a fixed bug. It is a cost the project has
% accepted and not fixed (D-0028 part 1): the `.opb` half is M1-T25 and the
% justification half is D-0028 itself. If it ever gets cheap, the numbers above are
% what changed -- measure with `bench/run_bench.sh`, which reports .opb bytes, .pbp
% bytes and verify seconds separately, because they do not have to move together.
%
% Zero prunings, zero decisions, one `pol`, no `rup`: the pairing model for the
% opposite shape is width_sat_depth.fzn, whose cost is search depth and which emits
% no `pol` at all. Do not read the two as the same measurement.
array [1..2] of int: coeffs = [1, 1];
var 0..999: a :: output_var;
var 0..999: b :: output_var;
constraint int_lin_eq(coeffs, [a, b], 2500);
solve satisfy;
